      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{68098a4626271974ef4d2775|full_name}\n\nThanks for your answer.\n\nThe first reason is that in places where there are a lot of friends—for example, at gatherings where an instance with over 30 people is created—people usually take photos. I’m only speaking from my experience in Japan here, but in most cases, people take photos. At that moment, no matter how careful you’ve been up until then, you’ll unpin your avatar so everyone can see it. Since there’s no need for anything to be moving in the photo, I’d like to keep it turned off. Depending on their settings, most of my friends have their avatars set to “Show Avatar” anyway.\n\nThe second reason is that while Imposter takes it too far, people who aren’t familiar with Physbone often leave way too much unnecessary motion in their avatars, or they get messed with by others and end up looking terrible—there are just a lot of issues that are hard to deal with.\n\nEveryone is already using the Safety Avatar Performance Rank to set limits, but I’m not sure if it’s working effectively, or if there’s a clear UI to toggle it on and off. For example, while there are limits on download size, I don’t think there are any restrictions yet on elements that put a heavier load on the CPU or GPU. Raycasts are the same.\n\nSo I thought that if there were at least a place to set a threshold for the number of PBs, it might make things more comfortable. What do you think? Am I getting my point across...?\n\nTranslated with DeepL.com (free version)",
